WEBVTT

00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:03.440
"Shikada Dagashi"

00:00:02.480 --> 00:00:05.900
Manager, this one is finished.
Could you take a look?

00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:06.870
Ah, okay.

00:00:07.230 --> 00:00:09.320
Wh-Whoa! This is...

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:11.280
You're fast! And good!

00:00:11.570 --> 00:00:14.700
Well, please let me know if
you see any issues with it.

00:00:15.030 --> 00:00:17.990
No, th-there's none!

00:00:17.990 --> 00:00:20.910
Sorry for the wait! I made some coffee.

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:24.670
I used the coffee maker that I brought
from the café, so it's authentic.

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:26.960
Thanks, Saya.

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:27.960
--I brought one for you too,
if you like, Miss Owari--

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:29.000
--Coconuts...
--I brought one for you too,
if you like, Miss Owari--

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:29.560
Hm?

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:34.170
A liquid metal slime joined my group...

00:00:34.550 --> 00:00:35.970
Hell yeah!

00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:37.680
Oh... I'm happy for you.

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:41.680
Manager, when's the time limit on Sunday?

00:00:41.970 --> 00:00:44.690
Let's see... Factoring in
the travel time by train...

00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:46.690
Nine in the morning!

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:47.530
Roger!

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:52.480
Okay. This one is finished!

00:00:52.480 --> 00:00:52.740
Thank--

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:55.530
Argh! A metal slime fled!

00:00:55.450 --> 00:00:58.370
"The day after tomorrow"
"Sunday"
"Review event!!"

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:59.120
Hey! Stop playing and go make some coffee!

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:00.410
Ow!

00:01:00.410 --> 00:01:01.120
"Saturday, December 14"

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:01.950
"Sunday, December 15"

00:01:06.830 --> 00:01:08.830
"The day after tomorrow"
"Sunday"
"Review event!!"

00:01:12.130 --> 00:01:12.840
Dammit!

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:13.260
Here.

00:01:14.590 --> 00:01:15.880
I made you coffee.

00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:16.790
Thanks.

00:01:17.470 --> 00:01:18.280
It's bitter!

00:01:18.590 --> 00:01:20.720
Of course it is. I made it black.

00:01:25.480 --> 00:01:27.230
"The day after tomorrow"
"Sunday"

00:01:37.610 --> 00:01:39.280
Hey, hurry up!

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:40.370
Wait for us!

00:01:40.370 --> 00:01:41.990
"We're closed today"

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:45.750
"Created by: Kokonotsu"

00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:47.500
"Spin!"

00:01:48.580 --> 00:01:50.670
F-Finished...

00:01:50.670 --> 00:01:52.650
We worked hard, didn't we?

00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:56.970
You worked really hard.

00:01:57.550 --> 00:01:59.680
I'm glad to see you got it done.

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:01.900
Coconuts...?

00:02:02.850 --> 00:02:04.220
Coconuts?!

00:02:04.220 --> 00:02:05.180
Manager?!

00:02:10.940 --> 00:02:12.810
H-He's a goner.

00:02:20.360 --> 00:02:20.950
My honey!

00:02:20.950 --> 00:02:24.080
That sugar feeling, sugar feeling,
when I take a bite

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:26.950
That sugar feeling, sugar feeling flows into me

00:02:26.950 --> 00:02:34.880
The crackling sparkle is giving me a sugar rush

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:40.220
I'm stuffed... I can't...
but I'm hungry for more!

00:02:40.220 --> 00:02:43.430
A scent drifts into the air...

00:02:43.430 --> 00:02:46.600
Could it be you?

00:02:46.600 --> 00:02:52.770
With those footsteps that sound like
a colorful and full candy box shaking

00:02:52.770 --> 00:03:02.660
I feel like I can reach that cotton
candy in the sky, but it's no good

00:03:02.660 --> 00:03:08.870
Don't melt away! Don't disappear!
I want to tell you my feelings!

00:03:08.870 --> 00:03:09.620
You're hungry?

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:10.160
My honey!

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:11.830
That sugar feeling, sugar feeling

00:03:11.830 --> 00:03:16.590
The first bite was full of mystery

00:03:16.590 --> 00:03:18.210
That sugar feeling, sugar feeling

00:03:18.210 --> 00:03:22.970
The second bite got me hopelessly addicted

00:03:22.970 --> 00:03:24.470
That sugar feeling, sugar feeling

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:29.310
The more I chew, the deeper the flavor

00:03:29.310 --> 00:03:30.930
That sugar feeling, sugar feeling

00:03:30.930 --> 00:03:36.820
Before I knew it, I was
completely crazy about you

00:03:36.820 --> 00:03:41.820
I'm stuffed... I can't...
but I'm hungry for more!

00:03:44.530 --> 00:03:47.490
Manager! You'll be late!

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:49.940
O-Okay!

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:00.010
"Meito Homerun! (Won 1 free bar)"

00:04:02.050 --> 00:04:05.550
Next stop is Hata... Hata.

00:04:05.550 --> 00:04:07.510
Please change trains for Nanyou Line.

00:04:08.970 --> 00:04:10.800
I-Is this the place?

00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:16.150
The On-site Manga Review Event venue
is at the bookstore in there, right...?

00:04:16.520 --> 00:04:18.810
Ah... I'm getting nervous.

00:04:19.900 --> 00:04:22.900
"Tenyoukai Bookstore"

00:04:23.900 --> 00:04:26.410
"Shonen Monday"
"Venue for the On-site Manga Review Event"
"Registration closes at 5:00"

00:04:24.570 --> 00:04:29.790
The reviews in this event are done by a
professional editor, right? It's scary.

00:04:29.830 --> 00:04:33.250
Yeah. I've participated several
times and it never gets any easier.

00:04:36.540 --> 00:04:37.880
Welco-- Ah!

00:04:38.340 --> 00:04:39.670
Welcome!

00:04:39.670 --> 00:04:42.380
Hey! How's it going?

00:04:43.220 --> 00:04:44.470
It's cold out there!

00:04:44.470 --> 00:04:47.140
Wow! You really are running a café.

00:04:47.430 --> 00:04:52.140
Thank you both for your
help yesterday, wait, I guess it was today!

00:04:52.770 --> 00:04:56.150
Well, all I really did was make coffee.

00:04:56.150 --> 00:04:58.400
And when it comes to my brother,
well, he literally did nothing.

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:00.460
Hey, hey, don't be ridiculous.

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:03.780
In just one day, I cleared FOUR games!

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:06.570
That's not "helping." It's screwing around!

00:05:06.570 --> 00:05:10.080
Well, having some background
noise makes it easier to focus, so...

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:11.080
Background noise...

00:05:11.620 --> 00:05:15.630
In any case, I wonder how things
will turn out for Coconuts.

00:05:16.170 --> 00:05:18.400
Even I'm getting nervous.

00:05:18.960 --> 00:05:20.170
Thanks for waiting.

00:05:20.170 --> 00:05:22.880
She's been saying that all day today.

00:05:23.170 --> 00:05:27.590
S-So what? Coconuts might become
a manga author, you know!

00:05:27.890 --> 00:05:29.880
I just can't calm myself down!

00:05:31.350 --> 00:05:32.460
Thanks for the coffee.

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:37.520
Oh, yeah. Maybe we'll celebrate
when he comes back.

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:41.300
You're getting ahead of yourself.
Isn't it more like a wrap-up party?

00:05:41.980 --> 00:05:47.540
Hmm... But I think it's
better not to do it today.

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:52.120
"Thump, thump, thump..."

00:05:48.280 --> 00:05:51.360
Ahh... I'm super nervous...

00:05:51.740 --> 00:05:53.320
Mr. Kokonotsu Shikada. Mr. Shikada...

00:05:54.660 --> 00:05:55.630
H-Here!

00:05:57.000 --> 00:05:59.040
Um... Is that because...

00:05:59.040 --> 00:06:03.260
I think he'll probably come
home feeling really bummed out.

00:06:08.680 --> 00:06:09.300
You...

00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:10.260
Y-Yes?

00:06:11.300 --> 00:06:15.350
You are amazing! At your level,
you can start a series right away!

00:06:15.350 --> 00:06:18.190
You could even win the best new manga award!

00:06:18.190 --> 00:06:19.520
What? What?!

00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:23.150
"A Promising Newcomer on the Rise"
"New Series!!!"
"Spin!"

00:06:20.810 --> 00:06:26.080
The manga Spin created by Kokonotsu-sensei
is a huge record-setting hit!

00:06:23.150 --> 00:06:26.440
"Spin!"

00:06:26.650 --> 00:06:28.280
--I love this manga!
--Despite the fact that it's been
published in a boys' manga magazine,

00:06:28.280 --> 00:06:29.150
--Kokonotsu-sensei is so cool!
--Despite the fact that it's been
published in a boys' manga magazine,

00:06:29.150 --> 00:06:31.200
--Kokonotsu-sensei is so cool!
--it's very popular among women, too.

00:06:30.360 --> 00:06:33.870
"The Japan Best New Manga Award"

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:34.910
The Japan Best New Manga Award
this year goes to...

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:38.620
"Kokonotsu-sensei / Spin!"

00:06:34.910 --> 00:06:38.250
...Spin created by Kokonotsu-sensei!

00:06:39.330 --> 00:06:42.080
Err... Thank you very--

00:06:45.380 --> 00:06:46.760
Ho...

00:06:53.600 --> 00:06:55.930
How long did it take to create this?

00:06:55.930 --> 00:06:58.060
Um...

00:06:58.060 --> 00:07:01.520
I started on it about three months ago...

00:07:01.520 --> 00:07:06.320
...but the actual time I spent drawing
was about two to three weeks, I think.

00:07:06.320 --> 00:07:07.900
About two weeks, I'm guessing?

00:07:07.900 --> 00:07:10.780
Um... Y-Yes, effectively...

00:07:10.780 --> 00:07:13.870
I see... That's pretty fast.

00:07:13.870 --> 00:07:15.870
Ah... well...

00:07:17.240 --> 00:07:19.580
I'm not lying or anything, right?

00:07:20.910 --> 00:07:23.210
Were you not able to spend more time on it?

00:07:23.710 --> 00:07:24.210
What?

00:07:25.380 --> 00:07:26.460
Um...

00:07:26.460 --> 00:07:29.050
I wish I could go over things page by page,

00:07:29.050 --> 00:07:32.550
"Created by: Kokonotsu"
"Spin!"

00:07:29.760 --> 00:07:32.550
but there are more people
after you, so I'll sum it up.

00:07:33.890 --> 00:07:36.060
You haven't learned how to budget your time.

00:07:36.600 --> 00:07:38.360
You have trouble focusing on things, don't you?

00:07:40.390 --> 00:07:44.480
Although you have a good feel for your strengths,
you avoid working on your weak points,

00:07:44.480 --> 00:07:46.390
so you're not making good use of your time.

00:07:46.900 --> 00:07:48.000
It's clear you're making excuses.

00:07:49.190 --> 00:07:52.520
I'm guessing that you did most of this
work over the past two days or so.

00:07:53.450 --> 00:07:56.870
Well, I give you credit for managing
to finish it by the deadline.

00:07:58.040 --> 00:07:59.760
If I am to mention one thing
you've got going for you...

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:02.880
...it's your youth.

00:08:06.590 --> 00:08:08.000
It ended in five minutes.

00:08:08.550 --> 00:08:10.420
It took me three hours to get here,

00:08:10.420 --> 00:08:13.010
and the review of my manga
ended in five minutes.

00:08:13.760 --> 00:08:17.760
Trouble focusing? Excuses?
What did he mean by "excuses"?

00:08:19.100 --> 00:08:21.310
I was busy with the shop.

00:08:21.850 --> 00:08:23.560
If I don't look after it...

00:08:24.520 --> 00:08:25.460
If I don't...

00:08:28.110 --> 00:08:30.320
Wait, why am I working as the manager again?

00:08:36.320 --> 00:08:37.830
"Meito Homerun! (Won 1 free bar)"

00:08:42.660 --> 00:08:46.330
Um... I'm sorry for saying
a weird thing like that.

00:08:46.330 --> 00:08:50.840
"Café Endo"

00:08:47.130 --> 00:08:50.840
No, I think I was getting carried away.

00:08:51.210 --> 00:08:54.480
I hope I'm just worried about nothing.

00:08:54.970 --> 00:08:55.590
Oh...?

00:08:56.840 --> 00:08:58.680
It's started snowing.

00:08:59.970 --> 00:09:05.600
Due to the snow, some trains have
been either canceled or delayed.

00:09:05.850 --> 00:09:11.690
It is currently unknown when the
delayed trains can resume service.

00:09:11.690 --> 00:09:12.860
Are you kidding me...?

00:09:12.860 --> 00:09:15.110
"Waiting Room"

00:09:25.870 --> 00:09:27.830
I wonder when the trains
will start running again...

00:09:29.460 --> 00:09:31.370
But I'm glad they're not running right now.

00:09:32.210 --> 00:09:34.630
Even if I could get home, I can't face Hajime.

00:09:35.720 --> 00:09:39.550
Saya and To... also went through
all that trouble to help me out.

00:09:50.860 --> 00:09:52.250
I wonder if I'm not cut out for it.

00:10:01.080 --> 00:10:01.650
Oh?

00:10:04.830 --> 00:10:06.210
If it isn't Kokonotsu...

00:10:14.760 --> 00:10:15.210
Ho...

00:10:21.300 --> 00:10:23.300
What're you doing in a place like this?

00:10:29.520 --> 00:10:32.660
L-Long time no see... Hotaru...

00:10:33.770 --> 00:10:35.860
It's been a while, hasn't it, Kokonotsu?

00:10:33.900 --> 00:10:38.030
"Homerun Bar Winning Stick, Snow, and..."

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:51.170
On that summer day,
we ate popsicles under the sun

00:10:51.170 --> 00:10:54.420
I still have the winning stick you gave me

00:10:54.420 --> 00:10:56.420
'cause I'm worried that if I take it to the shop

00:10:56.420 --> 00:10:58.720
even the memory will melt away like a popsicle

00:10:58.720 --> 00:11:00.880
I'm such a fool to think that way, aren't I?

00:11:00.880 --> 00:11:04.010
As the seasons pass, you get even taller

00:11:04.010 --> 00:11:07.180
The dream that was vague
has gotten a bit clearer

00:11:07.180 --> 00:11:08.850
When I felt kind of worried and held you tight

00:11:08.850 --> 00:11:13.650
you, with your eyes as sweet
as honey, smiled at me

00:11:13.650 --> 00:11:16.820
Festivals, fireworks, that hot summer

00:11:16.820 --> 00:11:19.990
Christmas, Valentine's, the freezing winter

00:11:19.990 --> 00:11:25.030
Let's spend the next season together, too

00:11:25.030 --> 00:11:26.330
"It's a promise, okay?"

00:11:26.330 --> 00:11:32.420
Adolescence? Who cares about it?
I don't care about forever, either

00:11:32.420 --> 00:11:39.210
Beyond the seasons gone by lies the future

00:11:39.210 --> 00:11:45.220
I wonder if this pain will go away someday

00:11:45.220 --> 00:11:55.360
That's what I was thinking as we ate the same
candy under the same sky on our way home

00:11:55.360 --> 00:12:01.990
I'm strange, aren't I? To feel
like it's a little bittersweet

00:12:07.950 --> 00:12:16.530
"Next time: 'I'm Back, Welcome Back, and...'"

00:12:09.040 --> 00:12:11.290
Next time. "I'm Back, Welcome Back, and..."

00:12:11.710 --> 00:12:14.090
Okay! I'm back, Kokonotsu!
